{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfukh7a5e6Vx8PVAsTQag","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I'm not aware of an official terminal chat client for Cloudflare Agents, though my knowledge may be out of date, so check the Agents docs and repo for a newer one. Agents speak WebSocket (and HTTP), so there are a few workarounds:\n\n- **Agents SDK client:** the `agents` package exports `AgentClient` (from `agents/client`), which works in plain Node. A short script that connects, sends messages, and prints the responses gives you a CLI.\n- **Generic WebSocket tools:** `wscat` or `websocat` pointed at `wss://<your-worker>/agents/<agent-name>/<instance-name>` work for quick testing, though you'll have to handle the message format yourself.\n- **MCP-exposed agents:** if your agent is an MCP server, you can use the MCP Inspector or `mcp-remote` from the terminal.\n\nI can write the small Node `AgentClient` script if you tell me your agent's URL and message format."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2250,"cache_read_input_tokens":535,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2250},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"da559d9b-a344-4461-9c57-2ebd7c50006d","uuid":"21575be1-71d9-4711-b722-f87ee701a6ae","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:39:21.880Z","request_id":"req_011Cfukh7PAknix7A2CU7bJe"}
